{"data": [{"author_id": "1017356438", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:27:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120251983265480932"], "id": "2120251983265480932", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120197861304598811", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z @generaltxn Congrats archi!", "url": "https://x.com/icefrog_sol/status/2120251983265480932"}, {"author_id": "2110211038469648384", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:18:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120249637747515443"], "id": "2120249637747515443", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120197861304598811", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z @generaltxn Localization is often treated as a final translation step, when it should be part of the product architecture from the beginning. Integrating it directly into the development workflow could save teams a lot of rework as they scale. I'm curious how they handle context and cultural", "url": "https://x.com/ARLPROTOCOL/status/2120249637747515443"}, {"author_id": "1708626733", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:14:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120233613136629901"], "id": "2120233613136629901", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1735371006578180096", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120213043569443144", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@generaltxn @a16z let's go!", "url": "https://x.com/katieschwartz/status/2120233613136629901"}, {"author_id": "1708626733", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:14:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120233575429931101"], "id": "2120233575429931101", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1735371006578180096", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120213043569443144", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@generaltxn @a16z 🫶", "url": "https://x.com/katieschwartz/status/2120233575429931101"}, {"author_id": "1948706120899674112", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:33:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120223443589247139"], "id": "2120223443589247139", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120197861304598811", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z @generaltxn localization going from a quarterly project to a react import is huge", "url": "https://x.com/humayun_x/status/2120223443589247139"}, {"author_id": "2102318912625094656", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:19:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120219795232841784"], "id": "2120219795232841784", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120197861304598811", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z @generaltxn The real win here is skipping the extract-and-sync dance with external TMS files. The hard part will be handling UI layout breaks when languages like German expand text by thirty percent.", "url": "https://x.com/JohnKocdr/status/2120219795232841784"}, {"author_id": "1437655880", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:05:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120216264257761436"], "id": "2120216264257761436", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120214703754670135", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2120197861304598811", "